{"kind":"article","metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"InnoRouterTesting"}],"role":"article","title":"Throttling Rapid Navigation Taps"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.swiftui\/documentation\/InnoRouterTesting"],["doc:\/\/com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.swiftui\/documentation\/InnoRouterTesting","doc:\/\/com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.swiftui\/documentation\/InnoRouterSwiftUI\/InnoRouterSwiftUI"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.swiftui\/documentation\/InnoRouterSwiftUI\/Tutorial-Throttling"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/innorouterswiftui\/tutorial-throttling"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Rate-limit navigation commands without threading timestamps through"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every call site. ","type":"text"},{"code":"ThrottleNavigationMiddleware","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" cancels commands that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"arrive within a minimum interval of a previously accepted command","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sharing the same key.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Scenario","text":"Scenario","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Users double-tap a “Buy” button. The first tap pushes the purchase","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"screen; the second should be silently dropped. Rolling that logic","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"into every button is noise — middleware is the right layer.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Installation","text":"Installation","level":2},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift skip doc-fragment","code":["let store = NavigationStore<AppRoute>(","    configuration: NavigationStoreConfiguration(","        middlewares: [","            .init(","                middleware: AnyNavigationMiddleware(","                    ThrottleNavigationMiddleware<AppRoute>(","                        interval: .milliseconds(300)","                    )","                ),","                debugName: \"throttle\"","            )","        ]","    )",")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The default initializer uses "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ContinuousClock"},{"type":"text","text":" and groups all"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"commands under a single global window. Within 300 ms of a previous"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"successfully executed command, the next one is cancelled. If the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"middleware is registered with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"debugName: \"throttle\""},{"text":", the surfaced","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reason becomes ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".cancelled(.middleware(debugName: \"throttle\", command: …))"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Per-command keys","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Per-command-keys"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Group throttle windows by the command’s identity or shape:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift skip doc-fragment","type":"codeListing","code":["AnyNavigationMiddleware(","    ThrottleNavigationMiddleware<AppRoute>(interval: .milliseconds(300)) { command in","        if case .push(let route) = command {","            return \"push-\\(route)\"   \/\/ each push route gets its own window","        }","        return nil                    \/\/ other commands pass through","    }",")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Return "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" to opt a command out of throttling entirely."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Testing-with-an-injected-clock","text":"Testing with an injected clock","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The middleware is generic over "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Clock"},{"type":"text","text":", so tests can drive time"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"deterministically:"}]},{"syntax":"swift skip doc-fragment","code":["let clock = TestClock()","let throttle = ThrottleNavigationMiddleware<AppRoute, TestClock>(","    interval: .milliseconds(300),","    clock: clock,","    key: { _ in \"all\" }",")","store.addMiddleware(AnyNavigationMiddleware(throttle), debugName: \"throttle\")","","store.send(.go(.home))","clock.advance(by: .milliseconds(50))","store.send(.go(.detail))         \/\/ cancelled — within window","","clock.advance(by: .milliseconds(400))","store.send(.go(.settings))       \/\/ accepted — beyond window"],"type":"codeListing"},{"text":"Composing with `.whenCancelled`","anchor":"Composing-with-whenCancelled","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A throttle cancel surfaces as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".cancelled"},{"text":", so","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".whenCancelled(primary, fallback:)"},{"type":"text","text":" treats a throttled command the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same as any other cancelled command:"}]},{"code":["store.execute(","    .whenCancelled(","        .push(.detail),","        fallback: .push(.home)","    )",")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift skip doc-fragment"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If the throttle middleware cancels the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".push(.detail)"},{"type":"text","text":", the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fallback "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".push(.home)"},{"type":"text","text":" is attempted next. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NavigationStore"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"routes that fallback back through the full middleware chain, so a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"global throttle key can cancel the fallback too if it still lands"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"inside the same throttle window. Each leg runs behind an internal"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"savepoint: if the fallback also fails or is cancelled, neither leg’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"partial state is committed."}]},{"level":2,"text":"Debounce?","type":"heading","anchor":"Debounce"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Debounce semantics — “wait N ms, then fire the latest” — live in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"DebouncingNavigator","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", not in "},{"code":"NavigationCommand","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". That keeps the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"engine synchronous while the async wrapper owns the timer,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"cancellation, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Clock","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" injection needed for deterministic tests.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Use throttle middleware for synchronous “reject too soon” behavior","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and ","type":"text"},{"code":"DebouncingNavigator","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for delayed “latest wins” behavior.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Next-steps","text":"Next steps"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"See ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.swiftui\/documentation\/InnoRouterSwiftUI\/NavigationStore-and-Hosts","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" for the typed ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onEvent"},{"text":" callback and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"NavigationStore.events","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" stream that expose throttle cancellations.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"See ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.swiftui\/documentation\/InnoRouterSwiftUI\/Tutorial-MiddlewareComposition","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" for the broader","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"middleware composition story (logging, entitlement gating,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"analytics).","type":"text"}]}]}]}]}],"references":{"doc://com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.swiftui/documentation/InnoRouterSwiftUI/Tutorial-MiddlewareComposition":{"type":"topic","role":"article","kind":"article","title":"Composing Middleware Across Navigation and Modal","url":"\/documentation\/innorouterswiftui\/tutorial-middlewarecomposition","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.swiftui\/documentation\/InnoRouterSwiftUI\/Tutorial-MiddlewareComposition","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Install logging, entitlement gating, and analytics middleware on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"both "},{"code":"NavigationStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"ModalStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Inspect the participant"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"discipline that pairs completion callbacks with the middlewares"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whose "},{"code":"willExecute","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" hook actually ran."}]},"doc://com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.swiftui/documentation/InnoRouterTesting":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.swiftui\/documentation\/InnoRouterTesting","type":"topic","title":"InnoRouterTesting","url":"\/documentation\/innoroutertesting","role":"collection"},"doc://com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.swiftui/documentation/InnoRouterSwiftUI/NavigationStore-and-Hosts":{"abstract":[{"code":"RouterHost","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the default self-contained stack-plus-modal surface."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"NavigationStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the advanced stack-only authority to use when the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"application needs to own navigation state outside a host."}],"url":"\/documentation\/innorouterswiftui\/navigationstore-and-hosts","type":"topic","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.swiftui\/documentation\/InnoRouterSwiftUI\/NavigationStore-and-Hosts","role":"article","title":"NavigationStore and hosts"},"doc://com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.swiftui/documentation/InnoRouterSwiftUI/InnoRouterSwiftUI":{"kind":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/innorouterswiftui\/innorouterswiftui","role":"collectionGroup","title":"InnoRouterSwiftUI","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.swiftui\/documentation\/InnoRouterSwiftUI\/InnoRouterSwiftUI","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Macro-first SwiftUI routing, externally owned stores, modal routing,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"coordinators, and typed "},{"code":"EnvironmentRouter","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" actions for InnoRouter."}]}}}